  ('kranjska-gora-slovenia', '01F', 'Kranjska Gora', 'Slovenia', 'Slovenia''s alpine corner', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Julian Alps / Slovenia', '{"ski","hiking","family","wellness","romance","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Slovenia''s premier alpine resort in the Julian Alps at the Slovenia/Austria/Italy corner; ski area 20 km pistes (10 easy/8 int/2 hard), 15 lifts, 807-1,282 m (475 m vertical), heavy snowmaking","Vitranc Cup Alpine Ski World Cup on the Podkoren slope since 1961 (65th edition 2025/26; GS + SL); first World Cup event in Slovenia/Yugoslavia 1968; record crowd 32,000 (1982); ranks with Adelboden + Alta Badia","Planica Nordic Centre: Gorisek Brothers ski-flying hill (Letalnica bratov Gorisek, HS225, built 1969), largest of 8 hills; hill record 254.5 m (Domen Prevc, 30 Mar 2025); 30 world records (29 men, 1 woman)","Ski Flying World Cup Finals close the season at Planica (next 17-21 Mar 2027); Nika Prevc women''s world record 242.5 m","Vrsic Pass 1,611 m (Slovenia''s highest road) via 50 numbered hairpins (26 south/24 north), built WWI by Russian POWs; Russian Chapel of St Vladimir (1915) at hairpin 8; snow-closed in winter","Lake Jasna: twin artificial lakes, 2.2 ha, on the village edge; up to 40 km groomed cross-country trails (Planica-Ratece-Tamar, 800-1,100 m)","Gateway to Triglav National Park (838 km², ~4% of Slovenia) + Mount Triglav 2,864 m, Slovenia''s highest peak; day lift pass ~EUR 49 (half Swiss/Austrian prices)"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (fire / ambulance / mountain-cave-avalanche rescue via GRZS, 24/7/365); 113 police","hospital":"Splosna bolnisnica Jesenice (Jesenice General Hospital) ~21 km; emergency ambulance stationed in Kranjska Gora year-round via 112","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"Alpine winter sports: off-piste avalanche risk (ARSO bulletin meteo.arso.gov.si + European 5-level scale; transceiver/shovel/probe + guide), cold/we