  ('laax-switzerland', '01F', 'Laax (Flims-Laax-Falera)', 'Switzerland', 'Europe''s freestyle capital', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Switzerland & the Alps', '{"ski","adventure","family","entertainment","wellness","ultra","romance"}', '{"alpine","adventurous","dramatic"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Flims-Laax-Falera run as one area by the Weisse Arena Group (since 1996), branded LAAX; Graubünden/Surselva","~224 km pistes (official Weisse Arena; J2Ski cites ~235 km - flagged), 28 lift facilities, ~70% of terrain above 2,000 m","Vorab glacier ~3,000 m top (lift-top ~3,018 m, summit 3,028 m); valley bases ~1,016-1,100 m","World''s largest halfpipe: ~200 m long x ~6.9 m high, since 2014/15 season (verified) - exceeds Olympic spec","Freestyle Academy = Europe''s first indoor freestyle hall (2010, ~2,000 m2, Laax-Murschetg): trampolines/airbags/ramps","LAAX OPEN = Europe''s largest snowboard event, annual since 2016 (successor to Burton European Open)","Snowparks led by NoName on Crap Sogn Gion (operator markets 5; German Wikipedia lists 4 - flagged)","rocksresort = Design Hotel apartment base at Murschetg gondola foot: 248 apartments, 8 restaurants, 6 bars, 9 shops; also Signina + Riders hotels","Waldwipfelpfad = world''s longest treetop walkway (1.56 km, opened 11 Jul 2021)","TWO federally designated in-area heli landing sites: Crap Sogn Gion + Vorabgletscher (FOCA/BAZL) - guided heli-ski genuinely servable","Own lift pass (not Magic Pass; no Ikon/Epic); reached via Chur rail hub + bus; Zurich ~1.5-2 hr (verify)"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 117 police / 118 fire / 144 ambulance / 1414 REGA alpine air-rescue / 145 poison","hospital":"Chur (Kantonsspital Graubünden) ~30-40 min; local practice for day cases; REGA 1414 alpine evac","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"Freestyle-park + glacier terrain — park injuries (jumps/6.9 m pipe walls: ride within level, helmet+back pro